title: Highlight* a mention that has body text or novel-to-the-target content.
pid: 6707d636-8983-4c28-9cdc-4ac4f029748f
body: |2-
    * here "highlight" = "include in the yellow number left of the '/' character"

  If the mentioner presents an atom that the target also (recursively) presents,
  that does not make the mentioner highlight-worthy in the target's link herald.
  (Stated differently, [[id:68715fd4-428f-4214-aa0e-2e76cd9898f2][presentation cons lists]]
  are not reason for a highlight in the target's link herald.)

  But if the nentioner has body text, or presents content that the target does not,
  that is reason to count the mention among the interesting mentions.

  The mentioner deserves an "interesting" highlight in the mentioned atom's herald
  becausee the mentioner is "saying enough about" the mentioned atom;
  since it might help them understand the metnioned atom,
  the mentioned atom's viewers deserve to be alerted.
